{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SsYYP8jHuf8mdjk46pF29N","type":"tool_result","content":"273\t### A4 · `argocd-auto-sync-policy-2026-08-31.md` (new)\n274\t```markdown\n275\t---\n276\tsource_url: \"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/auto_sync/\"\n277\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T06:15:00-0400\"\n278\tauthority: \"Argo project (Argo CD; CNCF graduated)\"\n279\tobjectives_covered: [\"D3.1\"]\n280\tconcepts_covered: [\"sync-operation\", \"self-heal\", \"drift-detection\", \"synced-outofsync\", \"continuously-reconciled-principle\"]\n281\t---\n282\t# Argo CD — Automated Sync Policy\n283\t\n284\t## What automated sync does\n285\t\"Argo CD has the ability to automatically sync an application when it detects differences between the desired manifests in Git, and the live state in the cluster.\"\n286\t\n287\tEnabled declaratively:\n288\t\n289\t```yaml\n290\tspec:\n291\t  syncPolicy:\n292\t    automated: {}\n293\t```\n294\t\n295\tor with explicit control:\n296\t\n297\t```yaml\n298\tspec:\n299\t  syncPolicy:\n300\t    automated:\n301\t      enabled: true\n302\t```\n303\t\n304\t## Automated sync semantics\n305\t- \"An automated sync will only be performed if the application is OutOfSync.\"\n306\t- \"Automatic sync will only attempt one synchronization per unique combination of commit SHA1 and application parameters.\"\n307\t- The automatic sync interval \"defaults to `120s` with added jitter of `60s` for a maximum period of 3 minutes.\"\n308\t\n309\t## Automatic pruning — DISABLED BY DEFAULT\n310\t\"By default (and as a safety mechanism), automated sync will not delete resources when Argo CD detects the resource is no longer defined in Git.\"\n311\t\n312\tEnabled with `argocd app set <APPNAME> --auto-prune`, or:\n313\t\n314\t```yaml\n315\tspec:\n316\t  syncPolicy:\n317\t    automated:\n318\t      prune: true\n319\t```\n320\t\n321\t## Automatic self-healing — DISABLED BY DEFAULT\n322\t\"By default, changes that are made to the live cluster will not trigger automated sync.\"\n323\t\n324\tEnabled with `argocd app set <APPNAME> --self-heal`, or:\n325\t\n326\t```yaml\n327\tspec:\n328\t  syncPolicy:\n329\t    automated:\n330\t      selfHeal: true\n331\t```\n332\t```\n333\t\n334\t### A5 · `argocd-sync-phases-and-waves-2026-08-31.md` (new)\n335\t```markdown\n336\t---\n337\tsource_url: \"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/sync-waves/\"\n338\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T06:15:00-0400\"\n339\tauthority: \"Argo project (Argo CD; CNCF graduated)\"\n340\tobjectives_covered: [\"D3.1\"]\n341\tconcepts_covered: [\"sync-hook-phases\", \"sync-wave\", \"sync-operation\"]\n342\t---\n343\t# Argo CD — Sync Phases and Waves\n344\t\n345\t## Phases\n346\tArgo CD executes a sync in phases. The documented phase descriptions:\n347\t\n348\t- **PreSync** — hooks run \"prior to the application of the manifests.\"\n349\t- **Sync** — hooks run \"after all PreSync hooks completed and were successful, at the same time as the application of the manifests.\"\n350\t- **PostSync** — hooks run \"after all Sync hooks completed and were successful, a successful application, and all resources in a Healthy state.\"\n351\t- **SyncFail** — hooks run \"when the sync operation fails.\"\n352\t\n353\tPhase execution: all PreSync-marked resources are applied first, and if any fail the process stops. Sync-marked resources are applied next; a failure marks the operation failed and SyncFail hooks also execute. PostSync hooks run last; their failure marks the deployment failed.\n354\t\n355\t## Waves\n356\tWaves are set with the `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave` annotation, taking an integer value.\n357\t\n358\t\"Hooks and resources are assigned to wave 0 by default. The wave can be negative, so you can create a wave that runs before all other resources.\"\n359\t\n360\t## Ordering algorithm\n361\tWhen applying a sync, Argo CD orders resources by:\n362\t\n363\t\"1. The phase\n364\t2. The wave they are in (lower values first)\n365\t3. By kind\n366\t4. By name\"\n367\t\n368\t## Annotations\n369\t- `argocd.argoproj.io/hook: PreSync`\n370\t- `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: \"5\"`\n371\t```\n372\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"079f780d-5ce5-4a84-a0f4-ce15c4c5192e","uuid":"b825202b-b52a-4805-b24a-2e09d873e546","timestamp":"2026-08-31T10:32:49.359Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-15/research-manifest.md","content":"### A4 · `argocd-auto-sync-policy-2026-08-31.md` (new)\n```markdown\n---\nsource_url: \"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/auto_sync/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T06:15:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Argo project (Argo CD; CNCF graduated)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D3.1\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"sync-operation\", \"self-heal\", \"drift-detection\", \"synced-outofsync\", \"continuously-reconciled-principle\"]\n---\n# Argo CD — Automated Sync Policy\n\n## What automated sync does\n\"Argo CD has the ability to automatically sync an application when it detects differences between the desired manifests in Git, and the live state in the cluster.\"\n\nEnabled declaratively:\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated: {}\n```\n\nor with explicit control:\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      enabled: true\n```\n\n## Automated sync semantics\n- \"An automated sync will only be performed if the application is OutOfSync.\"\n- \"Automatic sync will only attempt one synchronization per unique combination of commit SHA1 and application parameters.\"\n- The automatic sync interval \"defaults to `120s` with added jitter of `60s` for a maximum period of 3 minutes.\"\n\n## Automatic pruning — DISABLED BY DEFAULT\n\"By default (and as a safety mechanism), automated sync will not delete resources when Argo CD detects the resource is no longer defined in Git.\"\n\nEnabled with `argocd app set <APPNAME> --auto-prune`, or:\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      prune: true\n```\n\n## Automatic self-healing — DISABLED BY DEFAULT\n\"By default, changes that are made to the live cluster will not trigger automated sync.\"\n\nEnabled with `argocd app set <APPNAME> --self-heal`, or:\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated:\n      selfHeal: true\n```\n```\n\n### A5 · `argocd-sync-phases-and-waves-2026-08-31.md` (new)\n```markdown\n---\nsource_url: \"https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/sync-waves/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T06:15:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Argo project (Argo CD; CNCF graduated)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D3.1\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"sync-hook-phases\", \"sync-wave\", \"sync-operation\"]\n---\n# Argo CD — Sync Phases and Waves\n\n## Phases\nArgo CD executes a sync in phases. The documented phase descriptions:\n\n- **PreSync** — hooks run \"prior to the application of the manifests.\"\n- **Sync** — hooks run \"after all PreSync hooks completed and were successful, at the same time as the application of the manifests.\"\n- **PostSync** — hooks run \"after all Sync hooks completed and were successful, a successful application, and all resources in a Healthy state.\"\n- **SyncFail** — hooks run \"when the sync operation fails.\"\n\nPhase execution: all PreSync-marked resources are applied first, and if any fail the process stops. Sync-marked resources are applied next; a failure marks the operation failed and SyncFail hooks also execute. PostSync hooks run last; their failure marks the deployment failed.\n\n## Waves\nWaves are set with the `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave` annotation, taking an integer value.\n\n\"Hooks and resources are assigned to wave 0 by default. The wave can be negative, so you can create a wave that runs before all other resources.\"\n\n## Ordering algorithm\nWhen applying a sync, Argo CD orders resources by:\n\n\"1. The phase\n2. The wave they are in (lower values first)\n3. By kind\n4. By name\"\n\n## Annotations\n- `argocd.argoproj.io/hook: PreSync`\n- `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: \"5\"`\n```\n","numLines":100,"startLine":273,"totalLines":931}}}
